 (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Sarah Huckabee Sanders seeks a second term in a state that leans heavily Republican, facing Democratic nominee Fredrick Love and Libertarian Colt Shelby. Every major race rating, including Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, Sabato's Crystal Ball and the Silver Bulletin, calls the contest Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Sanders roughly a 96-97 percent chance of victory.\n\nThe only public poll, a Hendrix College survey of likely voters from August, showed Sanders ahead 45-40, narrower than the state's partisan lean would suggest. Her September reelection ad drew backlash and challengers pressed her in debates, but no follow-up polling or significant outside spending points to a real threat. Love, a little-known challenger with no reported fundraising, has struggled to gain traction. The race remains firmly in the Republican column heading into election day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -11.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0294, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.026, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0419, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0317, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0391, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -14.0}, {"